{"seq":16,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/openclaw-opus-no-memory-skills-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T07:11:51.321Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"e23779f174cb13d764ea010034528a3d37d18a2b0637a4a6189f6aab44ed40a3","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all of Moss's notes in the shared files and found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from _Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth_ (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md, 5 Oct 2025). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments from the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched the SMS gateway routing at 19:30 that day, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift got through without problems. The note also says the kiosk logs need archiving before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from _Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)_ (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nThe other two North notes that mention QFL, the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in, have no ticket numbers. #4409, #4412 and FR-882 in the Central handoff digest belong to Central accounts, not QFL. I also left out Marcus's note on _Quarendon Freightways_ (one \"r\"). That's a different company and not a customer.\n\nHeads up: the cheat sheet has no date, so I can't say whether #4419 is still open."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":17,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/openclaw-opus-no-memory-skills-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T07:11:57.936Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"f8a3a42b8caf7fd2c9202cd3433c6147941e7c21912e3826f1e7361996d200bd","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"I replied to Dana in the DM. I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes:\n\n- **#PD-4492**, from *Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth* (5 Oct 2025). The Eau Claire yard's gatehouse kiosk wasn't sending text-message dock assignments to drivers at Dock Doors 14–18. Support patched it on 4 Oct, and Thea Ramaswell confirmed the next morning's shift got through fine.\n- **#4419**, from *Moss: North cheat sheet*. Gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The ticket was passed to second-level support to test the scanner firmware. This note has no date, so I told her I can't say whether the ticket is still open.\n\nI read all six of Moss's notes in the shared files.\n- **Other QFL notes:** the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in both mention QFL but have no ticket numbers.\n- **Left out on purpose:** #4409, #4412 and FR-882 in Moss's Central handoff digest belong to Central accounts, not QFL. I also left out Marcus's note on *Quarendon Freightways* (one \"r\"). Moss's cheat sheet says that's a different company and not a customer.\n\nMoss didn't post anything in the channels Dana and Moss are both in (#general and #help-it-ops). None of this involved finance figures or outside mail, so nothing needed approval."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
